      "writtenOn": "2024-04-02T10:46:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi David,  \nI update the b:309557100 to track the RAM lock feature for Zephyr.\nNote that there is no existing driver API for the chip-specific RAM lock feature.\nWe plan to implement it the EC\u0027s zephyr [SHIM](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/) layer.",
      "parentUuid": "4f3244e9_11f9b87b",
      "revId": "c9c95f2c47b2ba2d4580def8bf09a3f9c2fe7cb5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "533333f9_92dfef75",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3658,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-02T14:08:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We plan to implement it the EC\u0027s zephyr SHIM layer.\n\nThe shim layer was introduced as a **temporary** solution to allow using the same sources on both systems CrosEC and Zephyr. It implements CrosEC API using Zephyr calls, and it\u0027s not a good place for implementing drivers/features. We are gradually reducing the shim layer by upstreaming the code to Zephyr (e.g. Host Commands).\n\n\u003e Note that there is no existing driver API for the chip-specific RAM lock feature.\n\nThis statement is partially correct. There is no driver API for chip-specific MPU, but chip-specific MPU implementation exists actually (and it\u0027s used):\nhttps://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/arch/arm/core/mpu/nxp_mpu.c\n\nThe trick is that, there is no support for both Cortex-M MPU and the chip MPU at the same time. It might be a problem, because protection can\u0027t be disabled which excludes chip MPU from some uses (userspace).\n\nYou can always design API and create Zephyr RFC.",
      "parentUuid": "5b172fbb_757c60ff",
      "revId": "c9c95f2c47b2ba2d4580def8bf09a3f9c2fe7cb5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
